data: {"task_type": "guideline_plus_eoh", "selected_sources": ["aasld_nafld_nash_2018", "aasld_portal_hypertension_2024", "acc_aha_afib_2019", "acc_aha_hfsa_hf_2022", "acr_ra_2021", "eoh_2025", "kdigo_anemia_ckd_2023", "kdigo_ckd_2024"], "reasoning": "The question requests a longitudinal mapping of multisystem organ involvement and damage including musculoskeletal, cardiovascular, hematologic, and hepatic systems in a patient with complex autoimmune disease (notably rheumatoid arthritis), cardiovascular comorbidities (atrial fibrillation, prosthetic valve), hematologic abnormalities (anemia, coagulopathy), and hepatic enzyme elevations. The 2021 ACR RA guideline is essential for musculoskeletal disease activity and treatment evolution. Cardiovascular involvement is best covered by the 2019 AHA/ACC AFib guideline and 2022 ACC/AHA/HFSA heart failure guideline given cardiac ICU stays and prosthetic valve. Hematologic issues including anemia in CKD are addressed by KDIGO 2023 anemia and 2024 CKD guidelines. Hepatic involvement and liver enzyme abnormalities warrant inclusion of AASLD 2018 NAFLD/NASH and 2024 portal hypertension guidelines. The internal EoH 2025 corpus is included to support integrated chronic multisystem disease trajectory modeling and shared decision-making beyond single-condition guidelines. This combination covers the major organ systems and disease activity, lab abnormalities, and treatment effects longitudinally as requested.", "step_id": "C2"}

